---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/11-08/',photo='https://camera.hamamatsu.com/content/dam/hamamatsu-photonics/sites/documents/99_SALES_LIBRARY/sys/SCAS0120E_C13440-20CU.pdf#page=1',outline='https://camera.hamamatsu.com/content/dam/hamamatsu-photonics/sites/static/sys/en/manual/C13440-20CU_IM_En.pdf#page=94';
---
<Layout pageTitle="ORCA-Flash4.0 V3 sealed exterior and offline image legend" description="Inspect the inactive Hamamatsu camera housing and read distances on an unrelated fixed checker drawing." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="orcav3"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/11-08/">← Equipment 11-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#or-evidence">References and checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">11-08 / INACTIVE CAMERA SHELL · DETACHED IMAGE LEGEND</p><h2>The graphic stays fixed. The ruler changes.</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect the closed ORCA-Flash4.0 V3 C13440-20CU. The separate checker drawing shows what a declared scale means for three fixed distances.</p></header>
<div class="or-cols"><section><h3>Inert C13440-20CU exterior</h3><canvas id="or-model" aria-label="Orbitable ORCA-Flash4.0 V3 shell and separate illustrated scale pad"></canvas><p id="or-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="or-front">Reset overview</button><button id="or-rear">Rear outline</button><button id="or-board">Detached legend</button></section>
<section><h3>Fixed offline checker graphic</h3><label>Authored ruler span<select id="or-span"><option value="diag">A · Diagonal marks</option><option value="row">B · One row</option><option value="same">C · Coincident marks</option></select></label><button id="or-next">Next span</button>
<div class="or-raster"><canvas id="or-raster" width="32" height="22" aria-label="Fixed synthetic checker image" role="img"></canvas><svg viewBox="0 0 32 22" aria-hidden="true"><line id="or-line" stroke="#ffc981" stroke-width=".32"/><circle id="or-dot0" r=".63" fill="#e9fff3"/><circle id="or-dot1" r=".43" fill="#ffc981"/></svg></div>
<p id="or-readout" role="status"></p><p>The optional markings sit above the same 32 × 22 pixels. The graphic legend is exactly 2 fictional units per pixel, with no camera scale or calibration.</p>
<button id="or-export">Download distance summary</button><p><a href={d+'example-graphic.json'}>Example ruler report</a>. The summary identifies its static source; it does not contain an acquired image.</p></section></div>
<section id="or-evidence"><h3>Selected case and verification</h3><div class="or-cols"><figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original front-quarter graphite ORCA camera with sealed silver ring and detached legend pad"/><figcaption>Original view. The <a href={photo}>Hamamatsu C13440-20CU cover photograph</a> establishes graphite cooling-rib shapes, round silver face and side projections. The ring is intentionally opaque and has no functional mount or sensor.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={d+'rear.webp'} alt="Original camera rear with sealed abstracted connector and grille shapes"/><figcaption>Original inferred rear. The <a href={outline}>Hamamatsu Ver. 1.9 outline, section 15‑1, printed p. 92</a> identifies the selected chassis and rear face. Surface detail and closed relief are inferred.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual / tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Primary case W × H × D</td><td>85 × 93.5 × 125 mm</td><td>Within 1 mm; side projections separate</td></tr><tr><td>Diagonal with 8 px and 6 px offsets</td><td>10 px · 20 graphic units</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><td>Horizontal 11 px</td><td>11 px · 22 graphic units</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><td>Coincident marks</td><td>0 px · same source graphic</td><td>Exact; unchanged raster</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Distance is the Euclidean separation of fixed pixel centers multiplied by the authored legend. No acquisition, image ingestion, images of tissue, calibration, illumination, working sensor or camera settings are represented. The register’s original equipment acceptance is unsupported.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'orca-v3.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'graphic.mjs'}>Static graphic and summary schema</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR target bounds</a>. Headset use not verified.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/11-08/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#orcav3 .or-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#orcav3 section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#orcav3 :is(button,select){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .25rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}#orcav3 button{cursor:pointer}#orcav3 :is(button,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#or-model{width:100%;height:354px;display:block;touch-action:none}#orcav3 .or-raster{width:min(100%,340px);margin:.45rem auto;position:relative}
#or-raster{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated}#orcav3 .or-raster svg{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%}
#orcav3 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#orcav3 figure img{width:100%}
#orcav3 table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#orcav3 td,#orcav3 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#orcav3 .or-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#or-model{height:282px}}
</style>
